      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `StringsComparatorTest_testLength.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-text/manual/testcases/StringsComparatorTest/StringsComparatorTest_testLength.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has two understandability issues:\n1. Parallel arrays (`before`, `after`, `length`, `lcs`) make it hard to see which inputs map to which expected value\n2. The `lcs` field is initialized in `setUp` but never used in this test\n3. The loop hides each individual case\n\nI'll rewrite using `@ParameterizedTest` so each case is self-contained and readable.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces the hard-to-follow parallel-arrays loop with a `@ParameterizedTest` backed by a `@MethodSource`, so each string pair and its expected modification count sit on a single line — making the intent of every test case immediately visible."
    }
  ],
  "last_code": "package org.apache.commons.text.diff;\n\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\nimport java.util.stream.Stream;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.ParameterizedTest;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.provider.Arguments;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.provider.MethodSource;\n\npublic class StringsComparatorTest_testLength {\n\n    static Stream<Arguments> stringPairsWithExpectedModifications() {\n        return Stream.of(\n            Arguments.of(\"bottle\",             \"noodle\",            6),\n            Arguments.of(\"nematode knowledge\", \"empty bottle\",     16),\n            Arguments.of(\"\",                   \"\",                   0),\n            Arguments.of(\"aa\",                 \"C\",                  3),\n            Arguments.of(\"prefixed string\",    \"prefix\",             9),\n            Arguments.of(\"ABCABBA\",            \"CBABAC\",             5),\n            Arguments.of(\"glop glop\",          \"pas glop pas glop\",  8),\n            Arguments.of(\"coq\",                \"ane\",                6),\n            Arguments.of(\"spider-man\",         \"klingon\",           13)\n        );\n    }\n\n    @ParameterizedTest(name = \"\\\"{0}\\\" vs \\\"{1}\\\" => {2} modifications\")\n    @MethodSource(\"stringPairsWithExpectedModifications\")\n    void testLength(final String before, final String after, final int expectedModifications) {\n        final StringsComparator comparator = new StringsComparator(before, after);\n        assertEquals(expectedModifications, comparator.getScript().getModifications());\n    }\n}\n",
